  "pre_registration": {
    "question": "Does the frozen R7-C5 (plus C4/C4b at 2 s) single-copy temporal-response curve predict the relative own-trial exposure effects of sliding-window training sets at benchmark level?",
    "evidence_status": "Lee2019 participants and recordings are those of C3/C4/C5 (not an independent cohort). Track A / Track B / C0 arms were never fitted. This is a prospective prediction of new pipeline endpoints on known participants, not a replication on independent participants.",
    "primary_scale": "correct-class probability points (C5's scale) for H2-H4; BA for H1; BA reported for everything",
    "H1": "Track A realistic contamination: L_s - G_s (BA) > 0 for each stride and model (Holm over 6). Context only; L and G differ in rows and held-out-run support (declared).",
    "H2": "Track B matched overlap effect: E(lag) - E(2000) for lag in 62..1000 and E(2000) (same trial, no shared sample) per model (p scale; Holm over 12). OWN vs OTHER match rows, class composition, held-out-run provenance, number of distinct held-out source trials and window offset; they do not match content.",
    "H3_trackB_primary": "Per model, participant retention rho(lag) = E(lag)/E(0) vs the frozen curve R(lag) (functional-free: one window per exposed anchor). Loss = sum over 6 lags of squared error; test D = L(baseline) - L(C5) > 0 vs OVL (shared-sample fraction), BIN (any overlap = copy) and EXACT (only copies leak); Holm over 6. Accuracy: 90 % CI of the cohort error within +/-0.10 at every lag (TOST, alpha 0.05).",
    "H3A_trackA_secondary": "Per model, q(s) = E_A(s)/E_X(s) vs the frozen PRIMARY additive functional sum R/(1+sum R) (first-order influence: effects of added rows sum) over lags s, 2s, ..., 2000; baselines OVL, CNT (count / density), BIN, EXACT in the same functional; Holm over 8. Nearest-lag and saturating functionals are reported descriptively and never used for a decision.",
    "discriminability_rule": "a comparison counts toward a classification only if prediction and baseline differ by >= 0.05 at some condition (computed from frozen predictions only).",
    "classification": "per model and track: CONTRADICTED if a discriminating baseline is significantly better; SUPPORTED_STRONG if C5 beats every discriminating baseline (Holm) and is within +/-0.10 everywhere; SUPPORTED_RELATIVE if it beats every discriminating baseline only; PARTIAL if some; else NOT_SUPPORTED.",
    "overall": "PREDICTIVE_TRANSFER_SUPPORTED if Track B EEGNet SUPPORTED_STRONG, Track B TS+LR at least PARTIAL and Track A EEGNet at least SUPPORTED_RELATIVE; PARTIAL_TRANSFER if Track B EEGNet at least SUPPORTED_RELATIVE; else NO_PREDICTIVE_TRANSFER.",
    "H4": "Curve swap: each model's own C5 curve predicts its Track B retention better than the other model's curve (2 tests); EEGNet - TS+LR retention at 62..1000 ms (5 tests; C5 predicts negative). Holm over 7.",
    "C0": "Conventional contextual benchmark (stride 500): random window-level vs trial-grouped 5-fold CV per participant; window-level, trial-aggregated and anchor-only BA; descriptive.",
    "guards": "retention ratios only if every participant's denominator exceeds 0.5 points (else declared fallback).",
    "inference": "54 participants; t95; two-sided MC sign-flip 1e6 (seed 10399); Holm within families.",
    "forbidden_after_any_fit": "changing a lag, stride, arm, functional, baseline, threshold, family, scale or participant set."
  },
